# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real file - .env is gitignored.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two URLs pointing at the same Neon database, differing only in the hostname.
#
# DATABASE_URL is the POOLED endpoint (hostname contains "-pooler") and is what
# the application uses. Each Vercel serverless instance opens its own
# connections, and Vercel runs as many instances as concurrency demands, so the
# unpooled endpoint runs out of connections well before anything else breaks -
# at which point every user sees errors, not slowness.
#
# DIRECT_URL is the UNPOOLED endpoint and is used only by Prisma migrations
# (see prisma.config.ts). The pooler runs PgBouncer in transaction mode, which
# has no stable session to hold the advisory lock a migration takes, so
# migrating through it hangs or fails confusingly.
#
# On a plain local Postgres with no pooler, set both to the same URL.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require&uselibpqcompat=true"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@host.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require&uselibpqcompat=true"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth (next-auth v5)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generate with: npx auth secret
AUTH_SECRET="replace-me"
